# MyNotes

Follow `docs/architecture.md`. Stay inside the current task scope. Do not add features, pages, libraries, or refactors the user did not ask for.

## Forbidden

- UI kits: Vuetify, PrimeVue, Element, Nuxt UI, and similar
- undo/redo libraries
- persist plugins (`pinia-plugin-persistedstate` and similar)
- `window.alert` / `window.confirm` — confirmations are custom modals
- storing 50 full note snapshots for history

## History

- Patch/command stack, max 50 entries, oldest dropped
- Text in one field coalesces to a single entry (commit on blur or ~400ms pause)
- Checkbox, add, delete are atomic entries
- A new change after undo clears the redo branch
- History lives in the editor session; save and cancel call `clear()`

## Hotkeys

Ctrl+Z / Shift+Ctrl+Z on the edit page. If focus is in an input/textarea and the current field has uncommitted typing, do not intercept (native undo). Otherwise `preventDefault` and use app history.

## Product

- UI copy is Russian; code, files, and commits are English
- TypeScript strict, Composition API, SCSS, Pinia without persist plugins
- Reusable UI goes into `app/components/ui`

## Git

Commit only when asked. Conventional commits, one concern per commit. No WIP messages.
